unit('introduction-motivation','main',1,'Opening paragraph','literature_context','Source motivates integrating quantum-dot and magnetic functions, noting size, composition, shape and long-range order as control variables. Prior submicrometre dimers used self-assembly and surface dewetting. Novelty and application statements belong to the authors’ 2004 context.',disposition='retain_cited_context',refs=['main-1','main-2a','main-2b','main-2c','main-2d','main-3a','main-3b','main-3c','main-3d','main-4','main-5a','main-5b','main-5c','main-5d','main-5e','main-5f','main-5g','main-6a','main-6b'])
unit('scheme-stages','main',1,'Scheme 1','scheme','Source diagram: 1 FePt → [FePt@S] 2 by S at 100 °C → [FePt@CdS] 3 by Cd(acac)2 at 100 °C → CdS–FePt 4 at 280 °C. Cutaway shells are the proposed morphology, not atomic coordinates or proof of an isolated intact intermediate.',assets=('scheme-1',),scope='1→2→3→4 reaction-stage labels')
unit('one-pot-mechanism','main',1,'One-pot overview and Scheme discussion','author_interpretation','Authors propose depositing amorphous CdS around FePt, then crystallizing CdS with heating; lattice incompatibility and solution surface tension drive dewetting to a heterodimer. The source does not measure a lattice mismatch percentage, interface structure, surface tension or an in situ dewetting trajectory.',disposition='retain_author_interpretation',assets=('scheme-1',))
unit('upstream-cited-fept','main',1,'Typical synthetic route paragraph; ref 4','upstream_context','FePt preparation is attributed to Sun et al. 2000: Fe(CO)5 thermolysis and Pt(acac)2 reduction by hexadecane-1,2-diol in dioctyl ether with oleylamine/oleic acid. This SI itself provides a working sequence; the separately cited Science paper has not been inspected in this task.',scope='FePt stage 1',disposition='retain_current_source_recipe_and_uninspected_external_reference',refs=['main-4'])
unit('no-intermediate-isolation','main',1,'Typical synthetic route paragraph','lineage','FePt 1 proceeds to sulfur deposition without separation or purification. Intermediate stages belong to the same one-pot sequence; the SI TEM samples require separate sampling/isolation whose detailed procedure is not reported.',scope='one-pot stages 1–3')

